# Opt-in marker for the worktree guard (existence is the whole check; content is
# never parsed).
#
# INERT, AND NOW INERT BY DESIGN RATHER THAN BY ACCIDENT.
# This marker is consulted solely in a repo's MAIN worktree; hive-pi is
# bare-repo + worktrees, so every checkout is linked and this never fires. It
# shipped that way in PR #19 and protected nothing until 2026-08-05.
#
# It used to be "kept as the fallback for a non-bare clone". That fallback is
# retired: since 2026-08-19 the guard ALLOWS a main worktree whose marker is
# COMMITTED, and says why. A tracked file arrives with every `git clone`, and a
# clone is a main worktree — so it could never mean "this directory is the
# anchor", and what it did instead was block every disposable clone anyone made:
# a rebase staging area under /tmp, a nested recovery clone, a sandbox's granted
# workspace. Four papercuts 2026-08-15..19, one blocking.
#
# To protect a checkout that really IS an anchor, create this marker UNTRACKED
# (one line in `<repo>.git/info/exclude`), the way `.worktree-pull-only` is done.
#
# What actually protects the anchor here is `.worktree-pull-only`, which the
# guard checks in a LINKED worktree. That file is deliberately **untracked** —
# one line in `hive-pi.git/info/exclude`, present only in the anchor checkout,
# exactly as hive does it. Committing it would put it in EVERY worktree and
# make every task worktree pull-only, which locks the repo against all work.
# (Confirmed the hard way: doing so blocked the very commit that introduced it.)
# The tracked-marker rule above is the same lesson, one branch over.
#
# hive-pi went bare-repo + worktrees on 2026-08-05, so ~/repos/hive-pi is gone
# and ~/repos/hive-pi__worktrees/main is a pull-only anchor. Work happens in
# task worktrees created with `gwq add -b <name>`.
#
# This repo has a second reason to protect that anchor, which the other guarded
# repos do not: ~/.pi/agent/{settings.json,mcp.json,AGENTS.md,skills,scripts}
# are stow symlinks INTO it. An edit there is not a dirty checkout — it is an
# uncommitted change to the live harness config of every pi session on this
# machine.
